 "category": "Leads and stabs",
 "text": "Sound: the bouncy, hollow organ stab of early-90s house and rave: short, punchy chords with a bright octave on top.\n\nHow it's built: a square (PULSE at 50 %) with a sine an octave up mixed in, through a mostly open filter; a short envelope with a little sustain makes the stab; Chorus and a Reverb. Six voices for chords.\n\nPlay: off-beat chords (minor sevenths sound right), short and rhythmic.\n\nTweak: the octave sine's level (mixer 2), the envelope's DECAY, the filter's CUTOFF.",
